#pragma once
// Structural mode (docs/structural-mode.md): checks the wiring of a binding term against one
// launch's memory-eliminated value IR, before the scalar-fold lowering (which contracts and
// reassociates across op boundaries, and interns equal recomputations into one node).
//
// The binding term is input data (schema sentryward.structural-term/v1), generated by the caller
// from the kernel row's declaration. Nothing here knows any op: an atom is either `primitive`
// (one PTX arithmetic operation of a named opcode and type, operands up to commutativity, through
// the conversions the term names) or `opaque` (only its operand leaf sets are checked).
//
// Per output element o of a term node n, three checks:
//  1. leaves: the input elements o's value DAG reaches equal the term's operands at o;
//  2. primitive: a primitive n's stored value is that operation on exactly the operand elements;
//  3. factorization: with the stored values of n's inner term nodes as cut leaves, o's DAG
//     reaches exactly those cut values (at the term's coordinates) and n's direct operands, and no
//     original input element by a path that avoids the cut.
#include <string>

#include "sentryward/value_analysis/memory_elimination.h"
#include "sentryward/value_analysis/unit_lifting.h"
#include "sentryward/value_ir/graph.h"

namespace sentryward::value_analysis {

// The JSON report of the structural check of `term_json` (the term's text) over `graph` after
// `memory` (complete). `lifting`: the graph holds only CTA class representatives (class mode, unit
// lifting): the check covers the representatives' elements, and each member by its per-allocation
// offset, which must be one whole row shift of every row-indexed object and zero for the others
// (the term's leaf patterns then shift with it). Null: every CTA is in the graph. Never throws on a term or graph mismatch: those are refusals
// in the report ("result": "matched" | "refused" | "unsupported"). `reference` (tests only): after a
// match, also report the role predicates' verdicts by a separate plain-reachability
// implementation ("reference": checks, holds, fails, undecided), for the differential test.
std::string checkStructuralTerm(const value_ir::Graph& graph, const MemoryEliminationResult& memory,
                                const std::string& term_json, const UnitLifting* lifting,
                                bool reference = false);

}  // namespace sentryward::value_analysis
